+    // Route a non-async event fired on an off-owner region worker outside a staging window back to the owning
+    // thread, where its plugin listeners run single-threaded exactly as under serial ticking. Chunk-system
+    // events can fire in the chunk pipeline rather than inside the random-tick/entity-tick begin/end window,
+    // so CURRENT is null and they would otherwise run inline on a worker thread. We hand the whole event off
+    // to the current region's mailbox via OwnerDomainExecutor.execute, a fire-and-forget enqueue drained by the
     // owner in postWorldTick(world).drainMailbox() once the parallel phase joins. It must be fire-and-forget:
     // the owner remains synchronously phase-bound and only helps owner-scoped region shards; it does not run
     // global callbacks until every world completes, so a synchronous round-trip would deadlock.
